# Security and build rules

- Never commit API keys, tokens, or secrets to the repository
- Use ScriptableObjects or environment variables for configuration
- Strip debug symbols and logging in release builds
- Use IL2CPP or CoreCLR for release builds (harder to reverse engineer than Mono)
- Enable code stripping to reduce build size
- Encrypt sensitive save data; never store plaintext passwords
- Validate server-side in multiplayer; never trust client data
- Use `Debug.unityLogger.logEnabled = false` in production or wrap in #if UNITY_EDITOR
- Obfuscate sensitive strings if targeting platforms where decompilation is a risk
- Verify package trust indicators for third-party packages (signed packages in Unity 6.3+)
